WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.440
- We both have very young kids.

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.970
Yours are two and six, right?

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:03.803
- That's right.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.730
- Okay. Are your kids musical?

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.533
- They are, yeah.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:09.893
They are.

00:00:09.893 --> 00:00:10.726
I think they're more talented

00:00:10.726 --> 00:00:12.240
than I ever was at their ages.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.201
You know what I mean?

00:00:13.201 --> 00:00:14.034
- [Kelly] You sound like a parent.

00:00:14.034 --> 00:00:15.539
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:15.539 --> 00:00:17.237
- They're, no, they're exposed to it

00:00:17.237 --> 00:00:19.440
so much more than I was.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.273
- [Kelly] Ah.

00:00:20.273 --> 00:00:21.106
- They're so much more comfortable

00:00:21.106 --> 00:00:21.939
than I was, you know? Yeah.

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:23.400
They're, they really, how
about yours? Are your-

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.380
- I, you know now that
you say that, I think

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.970
because they grow up around it, right?

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.200
So they don't know any different.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.940
So they've always seen
me, mommy, on stage.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.500
They've always come on stage
even when they were babies.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.570
So like, I think that they don't,

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.648
it kind of shakes off the
nerves a bit for them.

00:00:35.648 --> 00:00:36.481
- Yeah.

00:00:36.481 --> 00:00:37.920
- Yeah. Your voice is so magical.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.710
I was listening to you
earlier. Oh, it's so good.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.579
So what was like your
favorite song as a kid?

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:44.051
What's like, what'd you grow up-

00:00:44.051 --> 00:00:45.840
- Oh, you know, I remember
the first grown up song,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.070
I think we share this one.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:48.960
The first, the first grown up song

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.179
that I really liked was
Greatest Love of All.

00:00:51.179 --> 00:00:52.012
Whitney.

00:00:52.012 --> 00:00:54.600
- Did you, did you put
it on repeat in your room

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.560
and just keep belting it out?

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.393
- I did, yeah.

00:00:56.393 --> 00:00:57.917
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah. That's me.

00:00:57.917 --> 00:00:58.750
- Yeah.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.220
- Yeah. And my mom hated it,
like, it's paying off now,

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.300
but it was a lot of,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.707
we lived in a very
small duplex. (laughing)

00:01:05.707 --> 00:01:06.540
- Yeah.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.710
- Yeah. I don't think my
neighbors liked it either,

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.390
but it's like, her songs were so fun,

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:10.223
especially that one

00:01:10.223 --> 00:01:12.748
and the message, it makes you cry. Yeah.

00:01:12.748 --> 00:01:14.520
- What a message. I, yeah,
I remember there's this,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.600
there's this cassette tape

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.040
that I have from when I was a kid.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:17.880
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.230
- I had my own tape recorder in my room,

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:22.080
and I'm just doing that last, you know,

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.984
I'm just looping that the final chorus.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:28.317
♪ Greatest love of all ♪

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:30.900
- No prodigy. No prodigy.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.370
- And you, in your head,

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.548
you are Whitney Houston.

00:01:33.548 --> 00:01:34.381
- [Leslie] Oh yeah!

00:01:34.381 --> 00:01:35.550
- You were like, I am killing this.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:38.267
Yes. Oh my God. And they
had to listen to it.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.450
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.440
I love that.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.850
Did you ever do the,

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.260
'cause we're the same,
around the same age,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.390
did you ever do the, like play and record

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:46.980
to where you could record on your,

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:48.480
like, that was with my first demo.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:51.390
I did like the, you could kind
of mess with the tape on it

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.310
and then you could
record yourself on your,

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:54.450
so I recorded over people.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.860
I was like, I don't like
this anymore. (laughing)

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.510
- Oh yeah. I would do, I would do my own

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:58.450
background vocals, you know what I mean?

00:01:58.450 --> 00:01:59.850
- Oh, I was not that cool.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:00.960
- Oh yeah 'cause you could, like,

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.490
if you record it on this side,

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.077
then you put it on this side then record

00:02:04.077 --> 00:02:05.107
- [Kelly] Oh, the double. Yes.

00:02:05.107 --> 00:02:06.644
- Yeah. And then you'd
keep flipping, like,

00:02:06.644 --> 00:02:08.160
- You could get the
double for a minute. Yeah.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.270
That cost more.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.280
I was like, yeah, that
was, that's really cool.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.113
You were rich.

00:02:12.113 --> 00:02:13.249
So wait.

00:02:13.249 --> 00:02:14.297
(crowd laughing)

